- `{{ asset.path }}` ({{ asset.kind }})
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}
{% if supply_chain.changes %}

Dependency changes{{ " (truncated; the most significant are shown)" if supply_chain.truncated }}:
{% for change in supply_chain.changes %}
- [{{ change.kind }}] `{{ change.name }}` ({{ change.ecosystem }}{{ ", direct" if change.direct else ", transitive" }}){% if change.versions %} {{ change.versions }}{% endif %}{% if change.source %} · source: {{ change.source }}{% endif %}{{ " — " ~ change.note if change.note else "" }}
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}
{% if supply_chain.notes %}


Limitations and what was not checked:
{% for note in supply_chain.notes %}
- {{ note }}
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}

A dependency that only changed version, with its source and checksum intact, is
routine and not a finding. A change of source, a lost checksum, a mutable
reference or manifest/lock drift is worth reporting, anchored to the changed line
in the diff that causes it. Where something above says it could not be analysed,
that is not evidence that it is fine.
{% endif %}
